---
import PolicyLayout from "../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro";
import { business } from "../siteConstants/business";
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Delivery & Return Policy"
  description="How digital software development work is delivered, revised, accepted and cancelled. No physical goods are shipped."
>
  <p>
    {business.name} ({business.ssmNo}) provides digital software development
    services only. <strong>No physical goods are sold or shipped</strong>, so
    there are no shipping fees or courier deliveries. This policy explains how
    work is delivered to you and what happens if it is not right.
  </p>

  <h2>1. How work is delivered</h2>
  <p>Depending on the project, deliverables are provided electronically by:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Source code repository:</strong> access to, or transfer of, a Git
      repository (for example GitHub) containing the project code.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Deployment:</strong> installing the work on your hosting, server,
      cloud account or app store listing, or on hosting we agree in the
      quotation.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Files:</strong> documents, designs, builds or exports sent by
      email or a secure cloud storage link.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We notify you by email when each deliverable or milestone is ready for
    review.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Delivery timelines</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Estimated timelines are set out in the quotation for each project.
    </li>
    <li>
      Work starts once the deposit is received and we have the content, access
      and information needed to begin.
    </li>
    <li>
      Timelines are estimates. They may move if feedback, content or approvals
      arrive late, or if the scope changes. We will tell you as early as
      possible about any delay.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Review and revisions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Each milestone includes up to 2 rounds of revisions within the agreed
      scope, unless the quotation says otherwise.
    </li>
    <li>
      Changes outside the agreed scope are quoted separately before any work
      is done.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Acceptance</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You have 7 days from delivery to review each milestone and either accept
      it or send us a written list of issues.
    </li>
    <li>
      A milestone is deemed accepted if we receive no written feedback within
      that period, or once you start using it in production.
    </li>
    <li>
      Defects reported within 30 days of final acceptance that are caused by
      our work are fixed at no extra charge.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Returns</h2>
  <p>
    Because our work is digital and custom-made, it cannot be physically
    returned. If a deliverable does not meet the agreed specification, we will
    first correct it through revisions or defect fixes. If we cannot, you may be
    entitled to a refund under our <a href="/refund-policy">Refund Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Cancellation</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You may cancel a project at any time by notifying us in writing.
    </li>
    <li>
      On cancellation, you pay for work completed up to the cancellation date
      and any non-refundable third-party costs. Refunds of any balance follow
      our <a href="/refund-policy">Refund Policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      We will hand over all completed work that has been paid for.
    </li>
    <li>
      We may cancel a project if invoices remain unpaid or the project cannot
      proceed for reasons outside our control. In that case, you are refunded
      for any prepaid work not yet delivered.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Ownership and handover</h2>
  <p>
    Ownership of the project deliverables passes to you once all invoices for
    the project are paid in full, unless the quotation states otherwise.
    Third-party and open-source components remain under their own licences.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about delivery or cancellation can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> or see our <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
